# Aurelia House — Mediterranean Quiet Luxury

The site must feel expensive through **composition, not decoration**: an editorial layout warmed by Mediterranean materials and light. Reference `/styleguide` (`src/pages/StyleguidePage.tsx`) before designing anything new.

## Always
- Large immersive photography; full-bleed and asymmetric editorial compositions (`grid-editorial`, `layout-bleed`, `col-bleed-left/right`, `stack`).
- Big light Cormorant headlines (`text-display`, `text-h1`–`text-h3`) against small uppercase labels (`eyebrow`, `caps text-label*`) and Inter body copy (`text-body`, `text-lead`).
- Generous whitespace (`py-section*`, `gutter-x`) and thin hairline dividers (`Divider`, `border-line`).
- Warmth from material: `Section tone="sand" textured`, the default `photo-grade` on images, an occasional `shape="arch"` portrait image, one italic word per headline at most (`<em className="serif-italic">`).
- Palette tokens only: ivory, ivory-soft, charcoal(-deep), forest(-deep), gold(-soft), taupe, sand, white. Use tone-aware tokens (`text-fg`, `text-fg-muted`, `text-accent`, `border-line`) so dark sections flip automatically.
- Forest for grounding surfaces (menu, footer, occasional section); gold only as small accents.
- Square corners; 2–4px radius only where necessary.
- Motion from `src/lib/motion.ts` / `src/components/animations`: 500–1000ms, small travel, luxe easing, staggered text, slow image scale. Must respect reduced motion.

## Never
- Card-heavy grids, rounded cards, drop-shadow-heavy UI, SaaS/dashboard or generic hotel-template layouts.
- Hardcoded hex colours or new colours outside the palette.
- Bounce, rotation, flashy effects, neon glow, aggressive parallax, exaggerated hover animations.
- Ornament, crests, script fonts, heritage "old money" cues.
- Lorem ipsum or random placeholder UI.

## Accessibility
- Keep WCAG AA contrast: on ivory use `text-accent` (deep gold) / `text-fg-muted` (deep taupe), never raw `gold`/`taupe` for small text.
- Text on photography needs an overlay (`overlay="bottom" | "left" | "full" | "soft"`).
